  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Humanitarian Support to Vulnerable and Conflict-Affected Communities and Local Authorities in the Republic of Moldova</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under the proposed intervention,&#x202f;IOM will support the immediate provision of mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS) services to vulnerable host community, refugee, and third-country national families living in the Republic of Moldova. IOM will also support humanitarian border management and community security by strengthening the ability of the national police to maintain frontline border processing, security and stability through material and technical support in border areas and in areas of Moldova where large numbers of refugees are hosted.  Through this project, over 27,000 conflict-affected and vulnerable refugees, TCNs, and members of conflict-affected host communities in the Republic of Moldova will have improved access to humanitarian shelter, Non-Food Items (NFI), MHPSS services, and enhanced community security to address their urgent needs including through the winter.</narrative>
  </description>
